    {
      "talk": "Five marketing truths we can actually agree on",
      "spk": "Mark Ritson & Byron Sharp",
      "ven": "Debussy · Mon 22, 15:30",
      "buzz": 90,
      "sent": "pos",
      "read": "Two famous antagonists agreed, for once, on five fundamentals: mental availability does ~70–80% of marketing's job; distinctive brand assets are the mechanism (Ritson retired his own term 'brand codes' live on stage); sophisticated mass beats niche; brand purpose is largely nonsense; and consistency is undervalued — campaigns die at 30–40 days when they should run far longer.",
      "link": "https://www.thedrum.com/opinion/andrew-tindall-what-ritson-and-sharp-got-right-and-wrong-at-cannes"
    },
    {
      "talk": "Advertising in the age of AI",
      "spk": "Denise Dresser · OpenAI",
      "ven": "Debussy · Tue 23, 11:15",
      "buzz": 86,
